course: dictionary
lesson: 7845
title: Radiant: shining and glowing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, so use the clues around it to pick the right one. «Her radiant smile lit up the whole room.» A smile cannot give off light in the way a lamp does, so radiant here means full of joy, as if she is glowing.
explain: «The Sun sends out radiant energy: light and heat that travel through space.» In science, radiant means sent out as rays. The clue is that the energy travels, and that is a different meaning from a happy face.
explain: Astronomers also use radiant as a rare noun. «Meteors seem to fly out of one point, the radiant.» The radiant is the point in the sky where the meteors seem to start, even though they can streak across any part of the sky.
fact: Radiant means shining brightly, or giving off light or warmth.
fact: «A radiant smile» means a smile that shows joy, as if the person is glowing.
fact: «Radiant heat» and «radiant energy» are sent out as rays, like the heat from a radiant heater that warms you directly.
fact: In a meteor shower, the radiant is the point in the sky where the meteors seem to come from.
fact: To check your meaning, swap in «shining» or «glowing» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «Her radiant smile lit up the whole room.» What does radiant mean here? | *Shining with happiness, as if glowing | Stuck together | Dirty and untidy | Very cold
exercise: «The Sun sends out radiant energy.» What is radiant energy? | Sound that echoes off walls | A sleepy feeling after lunch | Water that drips from the roof | *Light and heat sent out as rays
exercise: In a meteor shower, what is the radiant? | The star pattern the shower is named after | The bright tail left behind by a meteor | *The point in the sky where the meteors seem to come from | The dust trail the Earth passes through
test: Nadia says radiant means rich. Is she right? | Yes, radiant means very expensive | No, radiant means quiet and still | *No, radiant means shining brightly, or glowing with joy | Yes, radiant means rich and grand
test: «Radiant with joy, she ran to meet her dad.» What does radiant mean here? | Covered in paint | Sent out as rays of heat | *Looking very happy and glowing | Very tired after a long walk
exam: «The meteors seemed to fly out from the radiant, yet they streaked across the sky.» What does the radiant mean? | A bright star at the top of the sky | The end of the meteor's path | *The point in the sky the meteors seem to come from | The name of the meteor shower
